WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.027
<i>PILOT [OVER RADIO]:
U.S. military escort CDC team...</i>

3
00:00:18.095 --> 00:00:20.668
<i>requesting permission
to enter Egyptian airspace.</i>

4
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.495
<i>MAN 1 [OVER RADIO]:
Permission granted.</i>

5
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.659
<i>PILOT: Dr. Scott.
off to the right. take a look.</i>

6
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.377
<i>He's on approach.</i>

7
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.045
<i>MAN 2 [OVER RADIO]: Visibility's good.
Time to target. three minutes.</i>

8
00:00:30.065 --> 00:00:32.940
<i>PILOT: Roger that. Two-two-zero.
MAN 2: Roger that. I see you.</i>

9
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.453
<i>PILOT:
Status. green.</i>

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.231
<i>Dr. Scott. prepare for landing.</i>

11
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.403
<i>Putting down close to the LP.</i>

12
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.374
<i>Twenty feet. 10 feet...</i>

13
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.060
<i>Wheels down.</i>

14
00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:49.750
<i>Doctor. you've got five minutes.</i>

15
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.582
[CROWD CHATTERING]

16
00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.740
<i>MEDIC: This way.
There are 6000 quarantined in this camp.</i>

17
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.861
We have 387 dead.

18
00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.546
My staff is down to six.
I thought you were bringing more doctors.

19
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.073
These are the latest
to come down with the virus.

20
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.054
Once the spots come. they die in two days.

21
00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.593
[PATIENTS COUGHING]

22
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.215
I'm sorry.

23
00:02:12.345 --> 00:02:15.064
<i>Make sure those snowmobiles
go to starboard Hangar F.</i>

24
00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.655
Chief Spurling. Chief Lewis. we are getting
underway at 1300. Let's pick up the pace.

25
00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.451
Yeah. I know all about
the Naval Mountain Warfare Unit...

26
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.244
but never heard of a dog
setting foot on a destroyer.

27
00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.793
- This isn't just a dog. This is Admiral Halsey.
- And he's a mean operator.

28
00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.475
<i>JETER:
Yeah? Well. so is the captain.</i>

29
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.629
<i>RACHEL:
You can just put that down over there.</i>

30
00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:54.854
Be careful. That's delicate equipment.

31
00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.433
I take it you're my new houseguest.

32
00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.622
I'm Commander Chandler. ship's captain.

33
00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.310
Rachel Scott. Sorry we had
to take over your helicopter bay...

34
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.869
but it was the only space large enough
to accommodate our lab.

35
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.710
I got 217 men and women on this ship.
Anything I should be concerned about?

36
00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.248
Oh. this? Uh...

37
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.986
This is just so we don't contaminate the work.
Not the other way around.

38
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.097
What exactly
are you gonna be studying up there?

39
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.556
- Birds.
- Birds?

40
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.028
We are virologists...

41
00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.753
tracking obscure microbes
in hard-to-get-to places.

42
00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.862
Pretty boring stuff. actually.

43
00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.837
We really do appreciate your assistance.
Captain Chandler.

44
00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.193
We're here to serve.

45
00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.965
Welcome aboard. doctor.

46
00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.549
<i>SLATTERY:
Hit it.</i>

47
00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.375
<i>JETER:
Roger that. Red deck.</i>

48
00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.727
Bird's chocked and chained.
Heading to the barn.

49
00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:22.659
Damn. it's cold. I can't feel my face.
Granderson. tell me. do I still have a face?

50
00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.067
Yes. sir. Though it looks like
you could use some lip balm. sir.

51
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.259
I should have taken that desk job in Miami.

52
00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:30.716
It is cold.

53
00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.777
<i>RIOS:
Captain's on the bridge.</i>

54
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.055
XO Slattery. let's see
if we can get your frozen ass back to Norfolk.

55
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.252
- TAO. Bridge.
- Bridge. TAO.

56
00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.131
<i>CHANDLER: Helo just dropped the target
for our final missile test.</i>

57
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:05.685
Target's 5 feet long. <i>2</i> feet wide.
and in the icy water has no heat signature.

58
00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.091
Let's find it and kill it.

59
00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.756
<i>WOMAN [OVER RADIO]:
Scanning for target. Scanning zone.</i>

60
00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:13.235
<i>MAN [OVER RADIO]: Kill track 5205.
WOMAN [OVER RADIO]: Target acquired.</i>

61
00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.252
- Target acquired. Break.
- Kill track 0845. aye.

62
00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.106
MSS. kill track 0845.

63
00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:19.622
<i>MAN:
Missile ready to fire.</i>

64
00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:25.188
<i>KARA: Missile clear.
SIEGLE: Two-two-zero-30. Thirty thousand.</i>

65
00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.383
<i>MAN:
Thirty-five.</i>

66
00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.442
[RADAR BEEPING]

67
00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.294
<i>- Boom.
SIEGLE: Target confirmed. kill.</i>

68
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.553
Good afternoon. Nathan James.
<i>This is the captain.</i>

69
00:05:41.605 --> 00:05:44.617
<i>After four very challenging months
at the top of the world...</i>

70
00:05:44.685 --> 00:05:46.747
<i>we have just passed our final test...</i>

71
00:05:46.925 --> 00:05:49.738
and I'm proud to say
you did it with flying colors.

72
00:05:49.845 --> 00:05:54.462
I'm asking the Pentagon if we can break
radio silence today to make calls and e-mail.

73
00:05:54.845 --> 00:05:56.743
Bravo Zulu to each and every one of you.

74
00:05:56.845 --> 00:05:59.693
Enjoy your success.
because we're going home.

75
00:05:59.765 --> 00:06:01.874
[ALL CHEERING]

76
00:06:09.365 --> 00:06:11.803
Gonna drop to 50 below.
Get them off the ice.

77
00:06:11.965 --> 00:06:13.043
<i>JETER:
Aye. sir.</i>

78
00:06:13.845 --> 00:06:15.854
<i>DANNY [OVER RADIO]:
Dr. Scott. come in.</i>

79
00:06:15.885 --> 00:06:17.373
<i>Dr. Scott. are you there?</i>

80
00:06:17.525 --> 00:06:18.721
<i>Please respond.</i>

81
00:06:19.085 --> 00:06:20.885
<i>Dr. Scott. come in.</i>

82
00:06:27.965 --> 00:06:29.746
You have got to be kidding me.

83
00:06:31.605 --> 00:06:35.490
We're so close. We need to make sure
the isolate isn't contaminated.

84
00:06:35.505 --> 00:06:39.074
- We need more samples.
- It's all right. We can come back tomorrow.

85
00:06:41.245 --> 00:06:43.226
Ma'am. we've been trying to reach you.

86
00:06:43.365 --> 00:06:44.818
CO wants you back on the ship.

87
00:06:44.925 --> 00:06:48.968
You can tell the captain
that I'll return when I'm ready.

88
00:06:49.045 --> 00:06:50.826
It wasn't an invitation. ma'am.

89
00:06:51.405 --> 00:06:52.418
<i>DANNY:
Right now.</i>

90
00:06:52.425 --> 00:06:54.371
<i>Captain's orders.</i>

91
00:06:55.045 --> 00:06:57.811
<i>MAN [OVER RADIO]: Landing checklist
complete. Gear down and locked.</i>

92
00:06:59.165 --> 00:07:03.811
<i>Twenty feet. 10 feet. wheels down.</i>

93
00:07:11.285 --> 00:07:14.953
- We can make it back for the Series.
- You don't think the Cubs are in it?

94
00:07:15.085 --> 00:07:16.983
<i>SLATTERY:
It's the weakest division in baseball.</i>

95
00:07:17.165 --> 00:07:19.556
- We were six games up when we left.
- That was June.

96
00:07:19.645 --> 00:07:20.805
And they're the Cubs.

97
00:07:20.965 --> 00:07:25.664
Captain Chandler. you had no right
to pull me from my work.

98
00:07:25.685 --> 00:07:28.204
- I'm gonna go check on the. uh...
- Yeah.

99
00:07:28.285 --> 00:07:31.625
Those men are here to support me.
You don't send them to bring me in.

100
00:07:31.765 --> 00:07:35.234
- Those men are sailors in the U.S. Navy.
- I say when I am done and ready.

101
00:07:35.285 --> 00:07:38.051
- I have finally found what I am looking for...
- Doctor.

102
00:07:39.805 --> 00:07:41.867
First of all. thanks for checking in.

103
00:07:42.045 --> 00:07:46.463
Think this is the first time you've said more
than three words to me since we left Norfolk.

104
00:07:46.565 --> 00:07:48.792
I am sorry
that I haven't had you over for tea.

105
00:07:48.925 --> 00:07:52.933
You know. your attitude was mildly charming
back in June. in Virginia...

106
00:07:52.965 --> 00:07:57.547
but up here at 50 below. when none of us
have talked to our families in four months?

107
00:07:57.605 --> 00:07:58.683
Not so charming.

108
00:07:58.805 --> 00:08:01.699
- Yeah. well. charm wasn't exactly my pri...
- Still talking.

109
00:08:01.805 --> 00:08:04.407
Now. I think I've been more
than a gracious host.

110
00:08:04.565 --> 00:08:08.280
Taxied you and your assistant around here
so you can chase after your ducks.

111
00:08:08.325 --> 00:08:10.060
- Arctic terns.
- Need to wrap it up.

112
00:08:10.245 --> 00:08:12.389
Our mission's done.
and we'll be heading back.

113
00:08:14.845 --> 00:08:16.708
I'll take a rain check on the tea.

114
00:08:23.645 --> 00:08:25.872
- Benzo. eat some fruit.
- Oh.

115
00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:28.443
Mr. Chung. it's our last night
at the North Pole.

116
00:08:28.605 --> 00:08:31.910
You got big plans. but don't you ever
get your head out of that book?

117
00:08:31.965 --> 00:08:34.859
- Nope.
- Okay.

118
00:08:38.725 --> 00:08:40.917
- Lieutenant.
- Lieutenant.

119
00:08:43.005 --> 00:08:44.657
Mm-mm.

120
00:08:50.845 --> 00:08:52.380
Danny. whoa.

121
00:08:54.525 --> 00:08:56.881
- Don't do that.
- Do what?

122
00:08:57.005 --> 00:09:00.145
- You know what that smile does to me.
- All's fair in love and war.

123
00:09:00.245 --> 00:09:01.616
Yeah.

124
00:09:03.165 --> 00:09:06.505
- Kara.
- We'll be home soon enough.

125
00:09:23.085 --> 00:09:24.538
<i>RACHEL:
Hello. are you reading me?</i>

126
00:09:24.685 --> 00:09:26.256
Come in.

127
00:09:26.405 --> 00:09:27.940
No. I cannot wait.

128
00:09:28.085 --> 00:09:30.312
This is Dr. Rachel Scott.

129
00:09:30.405 --> 00:09:33.382
I need to speak
to the National Security Adviser right away.

130
00:09:33.485 --> 00:09:34.563
You don't understand.

131
00:09:34.765 --> 00:09:38.433
My mission is being compromised.
I need more time to collect samples.

132
00:09:38.525 --> 00:09:41.502
We have a noisy channel.
I repeat. mission objectives achieved.

133
00:09:41.605 --> 00:09:43.140
We are ready to come home. Over.

134
00:09:44.685 --> 00:09:46.530
<i>MAN [OVER RADIO]:
That's a negative. commander.</i>

135
00:09:46.535 --> 00:09:50.635
<i>- The mission has been extended. Over.
- Extended? Why?</i>

136
00:09:50.655 --> 00:09:55.016
<i>Maintain radio silence and current position
until you receive further instructions.</i>

137
00:09:55.245 --> 00:09:57.718
<i>MASON:
Transmission terminated.</i>

138
00:10:15.605 --> 00:10:18.124
[BEEPING]

139
00:10:19.765 --> 00:10:21.909
What the hell is that woman doing?

140
00:10:38.165 --> 00:10:39.782
<i>RACHEL:
Quincy?</i>

141
00:10:39.925 --> 00:10:41.202
I think we've got it.

142
00:10:47.085 --> 00:10:48.456
<i>DANNY:
Sorry. man. Did I wake you?</i>

143
00:10:48.565 --> 00:10:49.761
[CHUCKLES]

144
00:10:49.925 --> 00:10:51.987
Doc told me to keep my distance.

145
00:10:52.125 --> 00:10:54.023
The admiral's scaring off the birds.

146
00:10:54.125 --> 00:10:58.004
- Sure it was the dog and not your breath?
- Heh. Whatever.

147
00:10:58.085 --> 00:11:00.147
Man. we should've been out of here
days ago.

148
00:11:08.245 --> 00:11:10.215
- What the...?
<i>MASON: Aircraft to position...</i>

149
00:11:10.225 --> 00:11:15.544
seven-six-decimal-three-five-north
- Zero-five-nine-decimal-five-eight-east.

150
00:11:15.645 --> 00:11:17.051
I have three... Make that five...

151
00:11:17.165 --> 00:11:20.423
unknown aircraft approaching.
range 24 nautical miles. 80 knots.

152
00:11:37.205 --> 00:11:38.530
Those are not ours. man.

153
00:11:38.725 --> 00:11:40.917
No. They're Russian.

154
00:11:58.045 --> 00:12:01.268
- Come on!
<i>RACHEL: We have to save the samples.</i>

155
00:12:01.365 --> 00:12:03.311
- Help me!
- Leave the box. Let's go.

156
00:12:03.445 --> 00:12:05.554
Rachel. leave the box.

157
00:12:18.365 --> 00:12:19.690
[GUNFIRE]

158
00:12:33.085 --> 00:12:35.312
[GUNFIRE]

159
00:12:35.525 --> 00:12:37.552
Let's go right now!

160
00:12:39.845 --> 00:12:42.318
Come on! Let's go! Come on!

161
00:12:45.685 --> 00:12:47.056
[RACHEL GRUNTS]

162
00:12:47.205 --> 00:12:49.186
<i>RACHEL:
Quincy!</i>

163
00:13:09.525 --> 00:13:10.685
Drop them. Drop them.

164
00:13:12.645 --> 00:13:14.016
[GROANS]

165
00:13:15.645 --> 00:13:17.707
[GUNFIRE]

166
00:13:22.005 --> 00:13:25.919
- Set General Quarters.
- General Quarters. Man your battle stations.

167
00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.499
<i>Transit up and forward starboard side.
down portside.</i>

168
00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:30.689
<i>Unknown aircraft approaching.</i>

169
00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:35.690
<i>MAN [ON RADIO]: TAO. Air. New air contact
80234 at 015 at 36.000 yards. Inbound.</i>

170
00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:37.193
TAO surface manned and ready.

171
00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:41.015
Deploy SCAT. CIWS to AAW Auto.
Hold fire on.

172
00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:47.866
[DOG BARKING AND GROWLING]

173
00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.468
[GROANING]

174
00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:56.722
[GROANING]

175
00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:00.360
<i>DANNY:
Take him alive.</i>

176
00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:06.044
- All engines ahead flank.
- Hard left rudder. All engines ahead flank.

177
00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.660
<i>MASON:
United States Naval warship.</i>

178
00:14:11.665 --> 00:14:15.626
Identify yourself and alter course
or you will be subject to defensive actions.

179
00:14:15.845 --> 00:14:17.041
Evaluate inbound missile.

180
00:14:17.245 --> 00:14:20.585
- Recommend launch chaff. Brace for shock.
- All hands. brace for shock.

181
00:14:35.645 --> 00:14:37.426
Take them out.

182
00:14:49.005 --> 00:14:50.083
Go to the 5 inch.

183
00:14:50.285 --> 00:14:52.969
- Surface TAO. kill track 5024.
<i>KARA [OVER RADIO]: Surface. aye.</i>

184
00:14:53.045 --> 00:14:54.580
<i>Guns. Kill track 5024.</i>

185
00:14:54.805 --> 00:14:56.047
<i>MAN [OVER RADIO]:
Guns. aye.</i>

186
00:15:07.365 --> 00:15:09.263
You Okay?

187
00:15:09.445 --> 00:15:11.589
- Clear!
- Come on.

188
00:15:20.345 --> 00:15:22.745
<i>CHANDLER: Where's Dr. Scott?</i>
- She's banged up pretty good.

189
00:15:22.765 --> 00:15:24.992
Doc's looking at her in Hangar 2.

190
00:15:27.085 --> 00:15:30.343
<i>CHANDLER [IN RUSSIAN]:</i>

191
00:15:32.045 --> 00:15:33.616
[SPEAKS IN RUSSIAN]

192
00:15:33.725 --> 00:15:35.296
What did he say?

193
00:15:36.445 --> 00:15:38.308
[IN ENGLISH]
The cure.

194
00:15:40.005 --> 00:15:42.149
He wants the cure.

195
00:15:48.845 --> 00:15:50.726
<i>SLATTERY:
All are accounted for. Are we at war?</i>

196
00:15:50.765 --> 00:15:53.988
Get me Fleet Forces. Get me NMCC.
If they don't answer. get me SECDEF.

197
00:15:54.085 --> 00:15:56.733
<i>SLATTERY: Supposed to be radio silent.
- Not anymore.</i>

198
00:15:59.345 --> 00:16:03.542
I told you I'm fine. Just hurry up.
Where's Quincy? I need my samples.

199
00:16:03.585 --> 00:16:06.680
You don't get your samples
until you tell me what's going on here.

200
00:16:06.685 --> 00:16:08.580
You have no authority over me.

201
00:16:08.585 --> 00:16:10.612
Everybody out.

202
00:16:10.805 --> 00:16:12.540
You need to hand that case to me.

203
00:16:12.585 --> 00:16:15.724
We may have just gone to war with Russia.
and they were after you.

204
00:16:15.725 --> 00:16:17.460
No more secrets.

205
00:16:17.805 --> 00:16:19.130
Tell me about the cure.

206
00:16:19.885 --> 00:16:21.330
I can't say anything.

207
00:16:21.335 --> 00:16:24.885
I swear to God. I will throw this overboard!
I want answers!

208
00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:28.082
You want answers?

209
00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:35.482
Seven months ago. outside Cairo.
there was an outbreak.

210
00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:37.921
A virus of unknown origin.

211
00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.154
Its genetic structure
was like nothing any of us had ever seen.

212
00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:45.802
It swept throughout the village.
killing everyone that it infected.

213
00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:49.475
Egyptian officials claim
the outbreak was contained. but it wasn't.

214
00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:52.264
Instead. it continued to mutate and spread.

215
00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:56.588
The CDC and the WHO
wanted to sample the virus...

216
00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.214
and the victims to create a vaccine.

217
00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:01.286
But nothing worked.

218
00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:06.166
It was my belief that we needed to find
the primordial strain here in the Arctic.

219
00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:08.207
The birds.

220
00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:10.613
They're just the carriers.

221
00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:13.464
They pick up the virus
from the melting permafrost.

222
00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:15.526
We finally found their feeding ground.

223
00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:19.790
- You have what you need to stop this thing?
- I won't know until we get it to the lab.

224
00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:21.683
We're running out of time.

225
00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:24.832
The virus is moving quicker
than any of us could have imagined.

226
00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:27.917
How would you know that?
We've been radio silent since Norfolk.

227
00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:31.160
Because I have my own satphone.

228
00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:35.108
We were at EMCON
so no one would know our position.

229
00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:40.370
We were at EMCON
to protect my mission. not yours.

230
00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:42.791
Orders came from the White House.

231
00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:46.613
Well. you led the Russians right to us
and endangered my entire crew.

232
00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:49.875
It was imperative I stay in contact
with the labs back home...

233
00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:51.878
to keep them informed of my progress.

234
00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:54.833
I don't think you understand
what we're talking about here.

235
00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.248
- Enlighten me.
RACHEL: When we left Norfolk...

236
00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:00.553
the virus was at phase two...

237
00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:04.825
limited to small clusters in Asia and Africa.

238
00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:08.479
We are now at phase six...

239
00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:11.051
global pandemic.

240
00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:15.563
Eighty percent of the world's population
is infected.

241
00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:21.343
The world is sick. Captain Chandler.

242
00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:23.560
Very sick.

243
00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:27.614
Are you telling me the whole world is dying.
and they sent two people to save it?

244
00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:32.724
It took weeks to convince the government
to even send me here.

245
00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:37.597
- Most of my colleagues think that I'm insane.
- Are you?

246
00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.362
I told you...

247
00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:45.729
that what's in that case
might be the only hope that we have.

248
00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:50.059
Captain? We have the president
of the United States on the vidcom.

249
00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.238
I'm sorry you had to find out this way.

250
00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:03.348
Can I have my samples now?

251
00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:12.246
<i>MAN [ON SCREEN]:
Stand by for the president.</i>

252
00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:16.136
<i>- Good morning. commander.
- Ma'am.</i>

253
00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:19.108
<i>I know. the last you heard
I was Speaker of the House.</i>

254
00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:22.172
<i>The president died two months ago.</i>

255
00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.444
<i>The vice president a week later.</i>

256
00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:28.628
<i>What's left of the federal government
is holed up 200 feet below the White House...</i>

257
00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:31.091
<i>and communication is getting spotty.</i>

258
00:19:31.220 --> 00:19:34.033
<i>So we need to know now:</i>

259
00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:37.773
<i>Does Dr. Scott have what she needs
to make a vaccine?</i>

260
00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.806
She thinks so. ma'am.

261
00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:42.706
<i>We are sending you the coordinates
to a secure bio-lab...</i>

262
00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.683
<i>on the coast of North Carolina.</i>

263
00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:47.511
Ma'am. we were just attacked
by the Russians.

264
00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:50.468
<i>Russia no longer
has a functioning government.</i>

265
00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:55.034
<i>From what we're hearing. a breakaway force
is operating on its own authority.</i>

266
00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:58.029
<i>We're still trying to ascertain all the facts.</i>

267
00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.496
Ma'am. our families.
how do we find out if...?

268
00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.344
<i>I wish I could tell you. captain.</i>

269
00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:08.890
<i>Most of our population.
including our Armed Forces. is dying or dead.</i>

270
00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:11.084
<i>We have no allies.</i>

271
00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:12.673
<i>We have no enemies.</i>

272
00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:15.995
<i>Just a world of sick. desperate people.</i>

273
00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:20.190
<i>Your ship was fortunate enough
to be out of the hot zone these past months.</i>

274
00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:25.914
<i>If Dr. Scott has the makings of a cure.
you have to come home now.</i>

275
00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.522
<i>MAN 1 [ON TV]:
Supply chains are completely broken.</i>

276
00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:37.483
<i>Food is in short supply. Hospitals are...</i>

277
00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:40.008
<i>WOMAN 1 [ON TV]:
Chinese government has detonated a bomb...</i>

278
00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.282
<i>on its own people
to stop the spread of the virus.</i>

279
00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:45.429
<i>WOMAN 2 [ON TV]: With possibly half
the world's population dead or dying...</i>

280
00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:49.034
<i>rumors that the U.S. is hoarding a vaccine
continue to swirl.</i>

281
00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:51.076
<i>MAN 2 [ON TV]:
Urban services are overwhelmed.</i>

282
00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:55.003
<i>In most cities. entire power grids are down.
making communication next to impossible.</i>

283
00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:57.738
<i>MAN 3 [ON TV]: The people are asking.
"Where is the government?"</i>

284
00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:00.576
<i>The virus has no treatment. no vaccine.</i>

285
00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:04.775
- So this whole weapons test...
- It was all just a cover.

286
00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:11.941
And EMCON Alpha. keep us in the dark
about what was going on at home.

287
00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:16.379
There's an unmanned refueling station
off the coast of France.

288
00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:19.221
If we operate at trail shaft.
we should just make it.

289
00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:22.503
How do we know they have fuel
to get us across the Atlantic?

290
00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.056
We don't.

291
00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:30.675
- What will we tell the crew?
- Everything.

292
00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:34.936
We tell them everything.

293
00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:45.228
Captain?

294
00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:46.530
The crew's assembled.

295
00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:55.104
Ship's company. attention.

296
00:22:09.170 --> 00:22:11.526
I have news...

297
00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:13.328
from home.

298
00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>MASON [OVER RADIO]: Any station this net.
this is Nathan James transmitting...</i>

299
00:22:32.690 --> 00:22:35.538
<i>in the blind on FLEETSAT one.
two and three. Over.</i>

300
00:22:35.610 --> 00:22:37.181
Is anybody out there?

301
00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:40.592
[LINE RINGS]

302
00:22:41.370 --> 00:22:42.448
[LINE BEEPS]

303
00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:44.843
<i>WOMAN [OVER PHONE]:
Due to widespread system failure...</i>

304
00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:48.938
<i>the number you are calling cannot be reached.
This message will not be updated.</i>

305
00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:51.032
[DIAL TONE HUMMING]

306
00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:53.008
<i>SAM:
Daddy!</i>

307
00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:56.927
<i>DARIEN: I can't believe I'm gonna go that long
without hearing your voice.</i>

308
00:22:58.970 --> 00:23:00.341
<i>ASHLEY:
I miss you. Daddy.</i>

309
00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:14.495
Captain's on the bridge.

310
00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:19.637
Sir. we're 50 miles off the coast of Europe...

311
00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:22.086
and still no contact
with French Naval Command.

312
00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:25.264
We've got extra watch and guns
at the ready.

313
00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:26.865
Were you able to reach home?

314
00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:29.503
No. sir.

315
00:23:29.690 --> 00:23:32.163
I think only four people got through
to anyone...

316
00:23:32.650 --> 00:23:35.334
and the news wasn't good.

317
00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.529
Last time we made port in France...

318
00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:42.658
I promised my girlfriend we'd come back
and see Paris together.

319
00:23:44.850 --> 00:23:49.925
With everything.
that's all I keep thinking about.

320
00:23:50.530 --> 00:23:52.639
Well. that's the stuff that matters.

321
00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:59.054
<i>JETER:
XO's on the bridge.</i>

322
00:24:01.170 --> 00:24:03.116
I got through to home.

323
00:24:04.370 --> 00:24:06.397
My boy's gone.

324
00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:08.578
Oh. Mike.

325
00:24:08.730 --> 00:24:12.984
Christine is up in Deer Park.
some sort of safe zone. for now.

326
00:24:13.210 --> 00:24:14.663
The girls are with her.

327
00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:16.791
- Why don't you take a break?
- No. no.

328
00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:19.656
I'm not gonna sit around my cabin
staring at the walls.

329
00:24:19.730 --> 00:24:22.707
- This is where I need to be.
- Sir? We have a fire order.

330
00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:26.718
It came across all channels. but it's garbled.
They cannot authenticate.

331
00:24:26.720 --> 00:24:29.274
[ALARM BLARING]

332
00:24:29.415 --> 00:24:32.263
<i>CHANDLER: Lieutenant?
SIEGLE: Confirmed order. Target's unclear.</i>

333
00:24:32.335 --> 00:24:34.889
Vampire! Vampire! Vampire!
Missile incoming high and fast.

334
00:24:35.055 --> 00:24:37.164
Spin four tomahawks.
Hold for target location.

335
00:24:37.255 --> 00:24:38.708
Coordinates don't make sense.

336
00:24:38.855 --> 00:24:40.590
<i>SIEGLE: No response.
- ECO. aye. Break.</i>

337
00:24:40.735 --> 00:24:43.548
<i>MM1. align four echo missiles
and place in the reload pool.</i>

338
00:24:43.655 --> 00:24:46.960
<i>CHANDLER: Do we have a target ID?</i>
- Now. five-one and trail.

339
00:24:47.055 --> 00:24:49.868
<i>KARA: Missile fired from a surface ship
in the North Atlantic.</i>

340
00:24:49.975 --> 00:24:53.233
<i>MAN 1 [OVER RADIO]: Ballistic missile
traveling at 9700 miles per hour.</i>

341
00:24:53.335 --> 00:24:55.673
<i>Confirmed. we have a nuclear bird in the air.</i>

342
00:24:55.755 --> 00:24:58.684
<i>KARA: We have no chance to intercept.
MAN 2 [OVER RADIO]: Batten down.</i>

343
00:24:58.735 --> 00:25:02.258
<i>Officer at the one. seal the ship.
Prepare for nuclear detonation.</i>

344
00:25:02.295 --> 00:25:03.537
<i>This is no drill.</i>

345
00:25:03.695 --> 00:25:05.839
Sir. the missile overshot us.
Headed for land.

346
00:25:10.655 --> 00:25:12.518
<i>MAN 1:
Detonation in 12 seconds.</i>

347
00:25:14.535 --> 00:25:16.597
[ALARM BLARING]

348
00:25:17.495 --> 00:25:20.179
<i>MAN 2:
Crew on the bridge. shield your eyes.</i>

349
00:25:21.335 --> 00:25:22.952
God help us.

350
00:25:40.695 --> 00:25:44.528
<i>CHANDLER: I need a status report
on the switchboard and generators.</i>

351
00:25:45.135 --> 00:25:46.460
- Who's that?
- Chung. sir.

352
00:25:46.615 --> 00:25:47.992
<i>CHANDLER: Anyone hurt?</i>
- No. sir.

353
00:25:48.055 --> 00:25:49.461
What's our engine status?

354
00:25:49.705 --> 00:25:52.880
Sir. the electromagnetic pulse
from the bomb blew our grid.

355
00:25:53.025 --> 00:25:54.513
Engines won't spin.

356
00:25:54.665 --> 00:25:57.138
No propulsion.
Emergency lights on battery power.

357
00:25:57.265 --> 00:25:59.656
<i>JETER: Captain?</i>
- That you. master chief?

358
00:25:59.785 --> 00:26:03.582
COMMO says the radios are down.
No way to get messages in or out.

359
00:26:03.665 --> 00:26:05.692
Move this ship away from the blast zone.

360
00:26:05.825 --> 00:26:08.673
Lieutenant.
let's get those engines back online.

361
00:26:08.825 --> 00:26:09.903
Yes. sir.

362
00:26:11.825 --> 00:26:15.375
- What temperature are we at?
- 41 degrees. We've lost negative pressure.

363
00:26:15.465 --> 00:26:18.805
- Damn it. We're gonna lose everything.
- Okay. get the ice.

364
00:26:20.265 --> 00:26:23.242
Fuses in. Open valves three. four and five.

365
00:26:23.305 --> 00:26:25.824
Shut valve to auxiliary engines
and emergency air.

366
00:26:25.945 --> 00:26:28.593
- Fuel lever on start.
- All right. give it a kick start.

367
00:26:30.665 --> 00:26:33.267
Sir. we only have one more fuse.

368
00:26:33.345 --> 00:26:35.899
Jet stream's pushing everything
north-northeast.

369
00:26:36.105 --> 00:26:39.034
We got a cloud of radiation
about to drop right on us.

370
00:26:39.505 --> 00:26:40.958
Give it to me.

371
00:26:41.145 --> 00:26:43.207
- Sir. it won't hold.
<i>CHANDLER: It'll hold.</i>

372
00:26:43.345 --> 00:26:45.701
- Captain. let somebody else do this.
- Rip it.

373
00:26:45.865 --> 00:26:47.892
- Get your hand out.
- Captain. don't.

374
00:26:48.025 --> 00:26:49.642
- Sir!
- I said. rip it!

375
00:27:02.745 --> 00:27:04.889
Bad-ass. captain.

376
00:27:05.625 --> 00:27:07.606
Bad-ass.

377
00:27:10.670 --> 00:27:14.010
<i>ALISHA: All engines ahead full.
Left full rudder. Steady on new course 270.</i>

378
00:27:14.110 --> 00:27:16.583
- What's our fuel percentage?
- Eleven percent. sir.

379
00:27:16.670 --> 00:27:19.764
Even at max conserve.
we'll run dry in six hours.

380
00:27:19.870 --> 00:27:22.929
- Any contacts on surface search?
- No. sir. 30-mile range.

381
00:27:22.990 --> 00:27:26.295
- What is that in the radar shadow?
<i>CHANDLER: Change range scale.</i>

382
00:27:26.390 --> 00:27:27.550
Looks like a ship.

383
00:27:27.670 --> 00:27:29.568
Calculate a course to intercept.

384
00:27:49.150 --> 00:27:51.588
<i>MAN [OVER RADIO]:
Markings indicate the ship is Italian.</i>

385
00:27:52.510 --> 00:27:56.143
- Bridge to Bridge operational?
- I think so. sir.

386
00:27:58.390 --> 00:28:01.648
Vessel in vicinity 48 degrees north.
15 degrees west...

387
00:28:01.790 --> 00:28:04.802
this is U.S. Navy Warship 151
on your starboard bow.

388
00:28:04.950 --> 00:28:07.258
Acknowledge and identify yourself. Over.

389
00:28:19.750 --> 00:28:22.844
Smith. Rowler. Benz. Green.
you're on provisions.

390
00:28:22.950 --> 00:28:25.258
Master chief.
you'll assist Chung with the unrep.

391
00:28:25.390 --> 00:28:28.484
We get as much food and fuel as we can.
and we get out.

392
00:28:28.630 --> 00:28:30.083
Let's move.

393
00:28:30.710 --> 00:28:34.543
<i>RACHEL: Remember. if the ship has been
impacted by the virus. it's airborne...</i>

394
00:28:34.590 --> 00:28:36.782
and highly. highly contagious.

395
00:28:37.470 --> 00:28:39.989
Even from a recently deceased corpse.

396
00:28:40.110 --> 00:28:43.532
You must keep your helmets on at all times.

397
00:28:44.550 --> 00:28:46.988
You trained for this. You can do it.

398
00:28:48.630 --> 00:28:50.528
<i>CHANDLER:
Send Naval Warfare to the kitchen.</i>

399
00:28:50.670 --> 00:28:52.651
Get as much food and supplies as you can.

400
00:28:52.790 --> 00:28:56.798
<i>DANNY: We got the stock rooms.
Benzo and I will make our way to the galley.</i>

401
00:28:56.950 --> 00:29:00.665
<i>JETER: Get that fuel line across and pump it.
- Sending the pull line.</i>

402
00:29:05.070 --> 00:29:07.297
<i>JETER:
Sending over the hose.</i>

403
00:29:07.950 --> 00:29:09.896
<i>CHUNG:
Feed the line.</i>

404
00:29:10.030 --> 00:29:11.272
Engineering. Bridge.

405
00:29:11.430 --> 00:29:13.411
<i>MAN 1:
Engage fueling.</i>

406
00:29:14.510 --> 00:29:16.537
System online. Commence fueling.

407
00:29:39.590 --> 00:29:42.484
<i>MAN 2: Ship's clear.
No one alive. Commander Chandler. Over.</i>

408
00:30:34.030 --> 00:30:36.092
[MAN SPEAKING IN ITALIAN]

409
00:30:38.870 --> 00:30:39.948
Dr. Scott!

410
00:30:42.190 --> 00:30:44.252
[CONTINUES SPEAKING IN ITALIAN]

411
00:31:01.070 --> 00:31:02.476
He wants help.

412
00:31:02.590 --> 00:31:04.734
The only thing that can help him
is morphine.

413
00:31:11.430 --> 00:31:12.801
Let go.

414
00:31:13.630 --> 00:31:14.790
Let go.

415
00:31:31.750 --> 00:31:33.731
Oh. shit!

416
00:31:33.830 --> 00:31:35.647
Benzo!

417
00:31:36.510 --> 00:31:38.081
Oh!

418
00:31:38.190 --> 00:31:39.268
Damn it.

419
00:31:39.990 --> 00:31:42.099
- Put your mask on.
- No. it's off!

420
00:31:44.310 --> 00:31:46.337
Oh. shit.

421
00:31:54.510 --> 00:31:56.491
Frankie. hey.

422
00:31:57.230 --> 00:32:00.405
Frankie. it's all right.

423
00:32:00.550 --> 00:32:02.285
Look. get up.

424
00:32:02.430 --> 00:32:04.786
Get away. man. Get away!

425
00:32:06.830 --> 00:32:08.776
Master chief. we're running dry here.

426
00:32:08.910 --> 00:32:11.183
- Engineering. Bridge. Disengage.
<i>JETER: Yes. sir.</i>

427
00:32:11.350 --> 00:32:14.279
- They've got it. Chung. Let's get out of here.
- Yes. sir.

428
00:32:14.390 --> 00:32:16.288
<i>DANNY: You're gonna be fine.
FRANKIE: Get away.</i>

429
00:32:16.390 --> 00:32:18.909
Just take the food
and go get the hell out of here.

430
00:32:19.070 --> 00:32:21.426
- I am not leaving you. Frankie.
- I'm a dead man.

431
00:32:21.550 --> 00:32:23.038
Just get out of here.

432
00:32:23.190 --> 00:32:25.463
<i>DANNY:
No. man. I'm not leaving you.</i>

433
00:32:25.550 --> 00:32:27.413
You tell him.

434
00:32:29.310 --> 00:32:30.552
He's been exposed.

435
00:32:30.750 --> 00:32:33.809
We put him back in his suit
and we quarantine him on the ship.

436
00:32:33.910 --> 00:32:36.969
You can't risk it. sir. Mission comes first.

437
00:32:37.470 --> 00:32:39.861
I'm not too interested
in dying like these people.

438
00:32:39.990 --> 00:32:41.232
Give me the gun. sailor.

439
00:32:41.910 --> 00:32:44.019
Frankie. don't be stupid.

440
00:32:44.110 --> 00:32:46.302
<i>CHANDLER:
I am giving you a direct order!</i>

441
00:32:46.470 --> 00:32:47.747
Put down that weapon!

442
00:32:47.910 --> 00:32:49.070
Frankie. no!

443
00:32:49.190 --> 00:32:50.761
[GUNSHOT]

444
00:33:07.510 --> 00:33:11.178
Lord God. by the power of your word...

445
00:33:11.270 --> 00:33:14.985
you stilled the chaos
of the primeval seas...

446
00:33:15.070 --> 00:33:17.801
made the raging waters
of the flood subside...

447
00:33:17.910 --> 00:33:20.676
and calmed the storm
on the Sea of Galilee.

448
00:33:20.790 --> 00:33:25.407
<i>As we commit our brother.
Franklin Edward Benz. to the sea...</i>

449
00:33:25.550 --> 00:33:28.316
<i>grant him peace and tranquility...</i>

450
00:33:28.430 --> 00:33:32.344
until that day when Franklin
and all those who believe in you...

451
00:33:32.950 --> 00:33:35.469
will be raised to the glory of new life...

452
00:33:35.550 --> 00:33:39.415
promised in the waters of baptism. Amen.

453
00:33:56.450 --> 00:33:58.185
<i>OFFICER:
Left face.</i>

454
00:33:59.885 --> 00:34:02.241
<i>Present arms.</i>

455
00:34:02.725 --> 00:34:03.803
Ready.

456
00:34:03.925 --> 00:34:05.003
[RIFLES COCK]

457
00:34:05.125 --> 00:34:06.238
<i>OFFICER:
Aim.</i>

458
00:34:06.365 --> 00:34:08.017
Fire.

459
00:34:08.365 --> 00:34:09.736
[RIFLES COCK]

460
00:34:10.020 --> 00:34:11.133
<i>OFFICER:
Fire.</i>

461
00:34:11.300 --> 00:34:12.378
<i>Ready.</i>

462
00:34:12.500 --> 00:34:14.035
[RIFLES COCK]

463
00:34:14.180 --> 00:34:15.258
<i>OFFICER:
Fire.</i>

464
00:34:15.380 --> 00:34:16.751
[GUNSHOTS]

465
00:34:29.900 --> 00:34:32.044
These people depend on me.

466
00:34:33.100 --> 00:34:35.913
I'm in uncharted territory here.

467
00:34:36.420 --> 00:34:37.498
We all are.

468
00:34:37.740 --> 00:34:39.017
Not you.

469
00:34:39.220 --> 00:34:40.755
You saw this coming.

470
00:34:40.900 --> 00:34:43.794
I never thought it would spread so fast.

471
00:34:45.700 --> 00:34:47.106
But now I know why it did.

472
00:34:48.260 --> 00:34:53.041
I compared the blood that we took from the
Italian to some samples I took before we left.

473
00:34:53.060 --> 00:34:54.712
The virus has an extra gene now...

474
00:34:54.820 --> 00:34:57.832
which could have only been added
with human intervention.

475
00:34:57.900 --> 00:35:00.338
So it was weaponized.

476
00:35:00.460 --> 00:35:04.831
Maybe. or maybe it escaped
from a lab somehow.

477
00:35:04.980 --> 00:35:06.632
But I think I know how to stop it.

478
00:35:07.300 --> 00:35:10.113
All the virus cares about is replicating.

479
00:35:10.260 --> 00:35:13.189
The engineered version lets it do that.
unchecked.

480
00:35:13.300 --> 00:35:15.327
So it no longer needs to mutate...

481
00:35:15.420 --> 00:35:17.811
which makes it stable...

482
00:35:17.940 --> 00:35:19.921
and easier to defeat with a vaccine.

483
00:35:20.100 --> 00:35:22.162
Then why hasn't anybody done that yet?

484
00:35:22.300 --> 00:35:26.097
Because they didn't have
the primordial sample.

485
00:35:27.740 --> 00:35:28.982
We do.

486
00:35:37.820 --> 00:35:39.437
[BEEPS]

487
00:35:42.260 --> 00:35:43.831
Bridge. COMMO. Get me the captain.

488
00:35:48.820 --> 00:35:51.714
Sir. we finally got the comms up.
This came through.

489
00:35:51.780 --> 00:35:52.893
A message from POTUS.

490
00:35:53.060 --> 00:35:55.908
- This is five days old.
- Transmitted while radios were down.

491
00:35:55.980 --> 00:35:58.336
We need to confirm these.
Get me the Pentagon.

492
00:35:58.460 --> 00:36:03.124
- Sir. I've been trying. but there's no answer.
<i>- I'll</i> try the lab. Get the presidential bunker.

493
00:36:04.980 --> 00:36:07.909
North Carolina's not safe.
President wants us to change course.

494
00:36:07.980 --> 00:36:11.941
There's a lab in Jacksonville that's secure.
No answer there or the Pentagon.

495
00:36:11.980 --> 00:36:14.253
Sir. nothing from the bunker.

496
00:36:15.020 --> 00:36:17.376
Signal's not getting out.
Checked the transmit side?

497
00:36:17.500 --> 00:36:20.054
That's not the problem.
Their phones are ringing.

498
00:36:20.180 --> 00:36:22.407
Sir. I have another message
coming through.

499
00:36:24.180 --> 00:36:28.551
It was transmitted at the same time
as POTUS: It looks like a much bigger file.

500
00:36:29.340 --> 00:36:31.238
- It's an mpeg. sir.
- Play it.

501
00:36:35.860 --> 00:36:37.560
<i>Tom.</i>

502
00:36:39.340 --> 00:36:40.911
<i>We're at your father's cabin.</i>

503
00:36:41.020 --> 00:36:45.555
<i>He thinks he has a way to get this message
out through his contacts at the Pentagon.</i>

504
00:36:46.020 --> 00:36:49.114
<i>I have no idea
when you might be seeing this...</i>

505
00:36:49.940 --> 00:36:52.084
<i>or where you are.</i>

506
00:36:53.380 --> 00:36:54.868
<i>We're all healthy.</i>

507
00:36:56.220 --> 00:37:00.181
<i>We managed to get out early and have been
up here for a couple months already.</i>

508
00:37:01.700 --> 00:37:07.231
<i>We haven't heard anything
from your brother or sister for a while.</i>

509
00:37:08.540 --> 00:37:10.028
My. um...

510
00:37:11.540 --> 00:37:13.111
<i>My sister didn't make it.</i>

511
00:37:14.900 --> 00:37:17.127
<i>But. honey. we're fine.</i>

512
00:37:18.100 --> 00:37:20.209
<i>We really are.</i>

513
00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:24.189
<i>And I really hope that you are too.</i>

514
00:37:25.060 --> 00:37:26.138
Oh. uh...

515
00:37:26.260 --> 00:37:29.319
<i>Kids. Come on out here.</i>

516
00:37:29.380 --> 00:37:33.177
<i>It's a tape for Dad.
Come on. Come. Come say hi.</i>

517
00:37:37.420 --> 00:37:39.647
<i>Daddy. where are you?</i>

518
00:37:39.780 --> 00:37:41.515
<i>We miss you.</i>

519
00:37:41.660 --> 00:37:43.852
<i>SAM:
We love you. Daddy.</i>

520
00:37:44.740 --> 00:37:47.998
<i>DARIEN:
Just get here if you can.</i>

521
00:37:48.100 --> 00:37:50.327
<i>We love you so much.</i>

522
00:37:51.140 --> 00:37:54.034
<i>Okay. All right.</i>

523
00:37:54.500 --> 00:37:56.481
<i>Let's turn it off.</i>

524
00:38:13.300 --> 00:38:14.952
<i>KARA:
Hey.</i>

525
00:38:16.940 --> 00:38:19.494
I don't know what we're going home to.

526
00:38:26.300 --> 00:38:29.722
No radiation detected
within a hundred-mile radius. sir.

527
00:38:29.780 --> 00:38:32.792
If America was nuked. it wasn't here.

528
00:38:34.140 --> 00:38:35.840
We're home.

529
00:38:49.580 --> 00:38:50.822
[LINE RINGS]

530
00:38:55.980 --> 00:38:58.828
You said you have what it takes
to make the vaccine.

531
00:38:58.980 --> 00:39:01.418
If you had to. could you do it here
on the ship?

532
00:39:02.820 --> 00:39:05.339
The lab wasn't built for that.

533
00:39:05.660 --> 00:39:08.473
- It's for collecting data.
- But if you had to. could you?

534
00:39:13.500 --> 00:39:17.461
The expeditionary team will forward deploy
and secure the area for the next group.

535
00:39:17.540 --> 00:39:19.438
Hopefully. we'll find support.

536
00:39:19.580 --> 00:39:21.115
Gotta be prepared for anything.

537
00:39:21.260 --> 00:39:23.944
Everyone carries their own bio-hazard suit.

538
00:39:24.020 --> 00:39:27.325
We do not engage unless we are engaged.

539
00:39:29.860 --> 00:39:32.544
Prepare your people. await further orders.

540
00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:34.235
Dismissed.

541
00:39:44.860 --> 00:39:48.118
Still no answer from POTUS
and nothing from Mayport or the lab.

542
00:39:48.220 --> 00:39:50.118
We can't even get an FM radio signal.

543
00:39:50.300 --> 00:39:52.444
If the power grid's down. everything's down.

544
00:39:52.580 --> 00:39:55.311
We'll know more
when we get boots on the ground.

545
00:39:55.860 --> 00:39:57.431
Mike. we're not going home.

546
00:39:59.020 --> 00:40:00.262
What are you talking about?

547
00:40:00.420 --> 00:40:02.612
The lab's 200 miles inland.

548
00:40:02.740 --> 00:40:04.767
You saw the news footage.

549
00:40:04.940 --> 00:40:08.115
- We'll fight our way in there if we have to.
- And then what?

550
00:40:08.220 --> 00:40:12.392
Generators run out in a couple of weeks.
Maybe civilian population tries to overrun it.

551
00:40:12.500 --> 00:40:15.313
- Too many variables.
- What do we do. we stay on the ship?

552
00:40:15.380 --> 00:40:17.653
Dr. Scott says she has what she needs here.

553
00:40:17.740 --> 00:40:20.717
We have standing orders from
the president of the United States.

554
00:40:20.780 --> 00:40:22.643
From five days ago.

555
00:40:22.740 --> 00:40:24.440
In the absence of command structure...

556
00:40:24.540 --> 00:40:26.978
I decide what's in the best interest
of our mission.

557
00:40:27.060 --> 00:40:29.908
And we have enough food here
to last us. what. a week?

558
00:40:30.060 --> 00:40:31.958
- How much fuel?
- We'll find what we need.

559
00:40:32.060 --> 00:40:34.204
- We'll die out there.
- No. we will not.

560
00:40:34.340 --> 00:40:38.711
Tom. I appreciate what you're trying to do.
It's not gonna work. People wanna get home.

561
00:40:39.060 --> 00:40:41.333
And who exactly gets to go home...

562
00:40:42.540 --> 00:40:46.548
when we have 80 bio-hazard suits
for 216 people?

563
00:40:49.580 --> 00:40:53.377
- We draw lots.
- I can't think like that. Mike.

564
00:40:53.460 --> 00:40:56.800
Give people a chance to get back
to their families. to say goodbye.

565
00:40:56.940 --> 00:40:59.331
I'm not letting anybody on this ship give up.

566
00:40:59.460 --> 00:41:03.714
- It's not your call. You don't get to play God.
- I'm still the captain of this ship.

567
00:41:04.340 --> 00:41:05.875
Now. I've laid out our mission.

568
00:41:06.940 --> 00:41:09.706
I expect you to fall in line.

569
00:41:19.780 --> 00:41:21.515
<i>RIOS:
Captain's on the bridge.</i>

570
00:41:33.460 --> 00:41:35.733
Left full rudder. All engines ahead flank.

571
00:41:36.140 --> 00:41:37.792
Sir?

572
00:41:39.340 --> 00:41:43.137
Left full rudder. All engines ahead flank.

573
00:41:44.660 --> 00:41:45.773
AYE. aye.

574
00:41:45.980 --> 00:41:48.207
Left full rudder. All engines ahead flank.

575
00:41:48.340 --> 00:41:50.402
<i>MAN: Left full rudder.
All engines ahead flank. aye.</i>

576
00:42:10.540 --> 00:42:12.275
This is the captain speaking.

577
00:42:13.140 --> 00:42:17.183
<i>[OVER PA] We have no contact with home.
and I have good reason to believe...</i>

578
00:42:17.260 --> 00:42:19.944
<i>the American government
is no longer functioning.</i>

579
00:42:20.060 --> 00:42:23.482
The country we all hoped
we were coming back to no longer exists.

580
00:42:24.060 --> 00:42:28.514
<i>We left these shores four months ago
as members of the United States Navy...</i>

581
00:42:28.540 --> 00:42:30.931
<i>but now we are more than that.</i>

582
00:42:31.020 --> 00:42:33.751
<i>Now our duty is to the entire world.</i>

583
00:42:34.660 --> 00:42:37.554
On board this ship is the hope...

584
00:42:38.540 --> 00:42:44.236
for our futures. for our families.
and for all humanity.

585
00:42:44.260 --> 00:42:46.533
Because in that lab in our helo bay...

586
00:42:46.700 --> 00:42:49.302
<i>are the ingredients for a cure...</i>

587
00:42:49.380 --> 00:42:54.209
and this is the safest place on Earth
for our scientists to do their work.

588
00:42:54.260 --> 00:43:00.565
<i>On a 3-billion-dollar piece of machinery
protected by 216 sailors in the U.S. Navy.</i>

589
00:43:01.180 --> 00:43:03.488
Our mission now is simple.

590
00:43:04.220 --> 00:43:07.935
We do whatever it takes to stay alive at sea
until they find that cure.

591
00:43:08.580 --> 00:43:11.920
<i>There's an unmanned food and fuel station
outside Guantánamo Bay.</i>

592
00:43:12.060 --> 00:43:14.662
<i>For the moment. that is our destination.</i>

593
00:43:18.580 --> 00:43:22.002
We've lost so much already...

594
00:43:23.420 --> 00:43:26.595
but this is the most courageous
and resilient crew with whom...

595
00:43:26.740 --> 00:43:28.802
I have ever been privileged to serve.

596
00:43:30.140 --> 00:43:35.004
<i>We will come through this together.
and we will prevail.</i>

597
00:43:37.820 --> 00:43:39.062
Carry on.

598
00:43:54.780 --> 00:43:56.515
Attention on deck.

599
00:44:01.820 --> 00:44:05.570
Lieutenant Granderson.
permission to salute the captain.

600
00:44:06.740 --> 00:44:08.392
Permission granted.

601
00:44:10.620 --> 00:44:12.016
And salute.

602
00:44:44.260 --> 00:44:46.516
[IN RUSSIAN]

602
00:44:47.305 --> 00:45:47.359
